From 8471fc322ab16e49710df7d5bc2522daec886a08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:08:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] linux/ppc: PIE via external linking, math/bits
 intrinsics, objdump support

-buildmode=pie is now supported for linux/ppc. 32-bit PowerPC has no
position-independent addressing mode, so the port keeps absolute
addressing under -shared and links PIE binaries externally; GNU ld
emits dynamic text relocations (DT_TEXTREL), which glibc's ld.so
applies. The FIPS relocation check is skipped for ppc for that reason.

Register the math/bits Len/TrailingZeros (cntlzw), RotateLeft32
(rlwnm), math.Abs (fabs) and math.FMA (fmadd) intrinsics for ppc.

Teach cmd/objdump about EM_PPC using the ppc64 decoder in big-endian mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0117Su2urNmg96oYM6vhHi1y
